course: dictionary
lesson: 7624
title: The word problem
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A problem can be a question you have to work out, like a maths story called a word problem. It can also mean something wrong or hard that needs fixing. «Read the whole problem first, then choose.» Read every word before you start, because the clues are often in the question at the end.
explain: When something is wrong, the word means a fault. «The car has a problem» means something in the car is broken or not working. Context helps: if the sentence also talks about fixing or solving, the problem is the thing that is wrong.
explain: In everyday talk, «What's the problem?» means «What is wrong?» Friends talk about their problems to help each other. Remember that «No problem» does not mean there is a difficulty. It means it is easy, or you are welcome.
fact: A problem is a question you have to work out, like a maths story.
fact: A problem is something that is wrong or hard and needs to be fixed.
fact: «No problem» means it is easy, or you are welcome.
fact: «Each new kind of transport solved a problem of the one before.» Here a problem was something hard that people fixed.
fact: Problem solving means finding a way to fix something hard, step by step.
exercise: «Read the whole problem first, then choose.» In this sentence, what is a problem? | *A question you have to work out | A loud noise | A kind of fruit | A sort of car
exercise: Sam says, «The car has a problem.» What does problem mean here? | A party with music | *Something wrong that needs fixing | A type of race | Something very pretty
exercise: Maya says, «No problem!» when her friend says thanks. What does she mean? | *You are welcome, or it was easy | She wants to play a game | She is very angry | She has lost something
test: «Each new kind of transport solved a problem of the one before.» What does solved a problem mean here? | Painted a picture | *Fixed something hard | Lost the way home | Ran very fast
test: Ben asks his teacher for help with a word problem. What is a word problem? | *A maths story you have to work out | A song about the sea | A list of colours | A map of a park
exam: Ella sees her friend looking sad and asks, «What's the problem?» What is she asking? | Which bus goes to town? | Does her friend like pizza? | *What is wrong? | How old is her friend?
